---
// All prose on this page is taken verbatim from the three Theseus Kickstarter campaigns.
import T from '../layouts/T.astro';
import { volumes, samples, links, MAIN_URL, shopUrl, priceRange, product } from '../data/theseus';
const options = ['theseus-the-full-collection', 'theseus-vol-3-hardcover', 'theseus-the-full-collection-digital'].map((h) => ({ h, title: product(h)?.title ?? h }));
---
<T>
  <section class="hero">
    <img class="hero-bg" src="/images/hero-theseus.jpg" alt="" width="2400" height="1350" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-txt">
        <p class="eyebrow">Jordan Holt</p>
        <h1 class="meander"><img src="/images/logo-large.png" alt="Theseus" width="1600" height="384" /></h1>
        <p class="lede">I’ve taken the narrative of his life directly from the ancient writings of Plutarch and spun it into a colorful, fully-illustrated, coming-of-age adventure both sincere and humorous.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a href="/read/1/" class="btn flame" data-continue>Start reading</a>
          <a href="#buy" class="btn">Get the books</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="story">
    <div class="wrap story">
      <div class="story-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">More About Theseus</p>
        <h2>This is most definitely not it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="story-copy">
        <p class="lede">Theseus is a well-known figure in mythology for defeating bandits, killing the minotaur, and ruling over Athens. While the story itself is a fable, there is likely a true story that undergirds the legend.</p>
        <p>This is more like what happens if someone loves Greek mythology very much, studies it in-depth along with the culture, language and history of that period, is fascinated by the idea of a true story behind the myth, but is simply not a serious person.</p>
        <p>This is a lovingly faithful retelling of the myth’s broader story according to Plutarch, but crafted into a compelling coming-of-age story garnished with ample humor and an unusually high number of interfering deities.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="wide"><img src="/images/crowd.jpg" alt="Theseus" width="2400" height="1080" loading="lazy" /></figure>

    <div class="wrap hero2">
      <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/ad-throne.jpg" alt="Theseus" width="1080" height="1080" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      <div>
        <h3>Young Theseus starts off like any teenager burdened with responsibility: he avoids it.</h3>
        <p>And rather than powerful hero from the myth, Theseus is neither very strong nor particularly smart, and is simply swept up in a tide of accidental fortunes as well as the schemes and mischief of a host of bored gods.</p>
        <p>But while encountering vicious bandits (each with their own brand of villainy) and mythological monsters, he begins the path towards a better and more capable version of himself...while still leaving room for humor.</p>
        <p>With his own legend outgrowing him, he’s forced to reckon with the man he aspires to be.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band light" id="books">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head-row">
        <h2>This is the complete Theseus collection, spanning nearly 500 pages.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Each chapter behaves like an independent episode, containing its own story but leading us further down the path of the over-arching tale.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vols">
        {volumes.map((v) => (
          <article class="vol">
            <div class="frame cover"><img src={v.cover} alt={`Theseus ${v.title}`} width={v.coverW} height={v.coverH} loading="lazy" /></div>
            <p class="eyebrow">{v.title} · {v.pages} pages</p>
            <h3>{v.hook}</h3>
            <p>{v.text}</p>
            {v.extras && <p class="muted small">{v.extras}</p>}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="spreads">
        {[1, 2, 3].map((n) => <figure><img src={`/images/spread-${n}.jpg`} alt="Theseus" width="680" height="680" loading="lazy" /></figure>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band dark">
    <div class="wrap tone">
      <blockquote>
        <p>“When you stand before a god of Olympus, it must feel like it.”</p>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="tone-copy">
        <p>This series is marked by its merger of mythology and comedy. Even with high dramatic stakes of Vol. 3, humor reminiscent of <em>Avatar: The Last Airbender</em> and even shows like <em>Futurama</em> is balanced with sincere drama. It’s not an attempt at subversion, but of solid storytelling.</p>
        <p>But this humor is never held at the expense of stakes, scale, and the wonder of encountering the beauty and strangeness of Greek myth.</p>
        <p>Along the way, Theseus also encounters the Immortals of the Greek Pantheon, clashing with, or cooperating with, the gods and goddesses of myth, each given a unique spin in his or her role to play in the tale.</p>
        <p>Along the way Theseus meets a colorful cast of characters, creatures and monsters, which give every chapter its own unique feel and provide ample surprises and discoveries for those who know Greek mythology. But even if you don’t, there’s humor, growth and soul to be found.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap trio">
      {['ad-kraken', 'ad-boar', 'ad-spear'].map((n) => <figure class="frame"><img src={`/images/${n}.jpg`} alt="Theseus" width="1080" height="1080" loading="lazy" /></figure>)}
    </div>
    <div class="wrap influences">
      <p>Major inspirations for this project were things like <em>Futurama</em>, P.G. Wodehouse, <em>Avatar: The Last Airbender</em>, <em>The Emperor’s New Groove</em>, <em>Legend of Zelda</em> and of course all of my favorite works of antiquity by Homer, Ovid, Plutarch, Babrius and Phaedrus, Virgil, Aeschylus and Herodotus.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="pages">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head-row">
        <h2>Here, have a couple of pages.</h2>
        <p class="muted">I enjoy the humor, but I also love trying to inject visually striking illustration and vibrant color into every spread.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="samples" data-gal>
        {samples.map((s, i) => (
          <button class="frame sample" data-i={i} aria-label={`Enlarge ${s.alt}`}><img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} width={s.w} height={s.h} loading="lazy" /></button>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="read-cta">
        <a href="/read/1/" class="btn flame" data-continue>Start reading</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band light buy" id="buy">
    <div class="wrap buy-grid">
      <div class="buy-imgs">
        <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/slipcase-front.jpg" alt="Theseus: The Full Collection" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/slipcase-back.jpg" alt="Theseus: The Full Collection" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </div>
      <div class="buy-txt">
        <h2>All of Theseus</h2>
        <p>For the first time since I began in 2020 the entire series is available to readers. For those who already have Vol. 1 &amp; 2, the final volume is here. For new readers and mythology lovers, you can get the full hardcover series here too.</p>
        <ul class="options">
          {options.map((o) => <li><a href={shopUrl(o.h)}><b>{o.title}</b><span class="price">{priceRange(o.h)}</span></a></li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band for">
    <div class="wrap for-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="lede">I know the temptation for creators is to say their work is for everyone. And as much as I hope it will be, here’s my best estimation of the core audience that this is written for:</p>
        <ul class="aud">
          <li>Those who love Greek mythology and don’t take themselves too seriously</li>
          <li>Those who enjoy endless humor, a good (or bad) pun and share my philosophy that there’s no such thing as a plot-hole, just an opportunity for a joke.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Is it for kids?</h3>
        <p>Safe for all ages! Younger kids may not pick up every word of the vocabulary, but in my experience this comic plays beautifully with those aged 10 and up. I would rate its content at PG. Two things I loved as a kid were comics and Greek mythology, so if you pick up a copy for one of the young people, that makes me very happy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band dark" id="creator">
    <div class="wrap creator">
      <div class="photos">
        <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/shipping-truck.jpg" alt="Theseus books ready to ship" width="1241" height="931" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        <figure class="frame"><img src="/images/book-vol1-photo.jpg" alt="Theseus Volume 1 hardcover" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About the Author</p>
        <h2>Jordan Holt</h2>
        <p class="lede">I draw primarily historical, mythological, religious, and literary works. I publish my own works and work with other publishers.</p>
        <p>I’ve worked in media, advertising, commercial illustration and held a faculty position at a university now for over 10 years.</p>
        <p>Theseus is a long-standing passion project for me. I started this project in 2020 at the start of the pandemic lockdown. These graphic novels are written, meticulously hand-drawn and colored by me, Jordan Holt. I don’t use AI in any form. I’ve spent about 1000 very pleasant hours writing and illustrating Volume 1.</p>
        <p>My little company, Carthage, is not big. It’s just me and the help my wife generously gives. We are truly an indie operation.</p>
        <p>My next book after Theseus will be an Anglo-Saxon penance fable called PetraCor.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a href={MAIN_URL} class="btn">Portfolio ↗</a>
          <a href={links.substack} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">Substack ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="lb" data-lb hidden role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Page viewer">
    <button class="lb-x" data-x>Close ✕</button>
    <button class="lb-nav prev" data-p aria-label="Previous page">‹</button>
    <img data-img alt="" />
    <button class="lb-nav next" data-n aria-label="Next page">›</button>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" data-samples set:html={JSON.stringify(samples)} />
</T>

<style>
  .hero { position: relative; min-height: min(86vh, 860px); display: flex; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; background: var(--deep); margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--header)); padding-top: var(--header); }
  .hero-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 78% 30%; }
  .hero::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(24,22,42,.96) 0%, rgba(24,22,42,.86) 34%, rgba(24,22,42,.25) 62%, rgba(24,22,42,0) 80%), linear-gradient(0deg, var(--night) 0%, rgba(33,30,51,0) 22%); }
  .hero-grid { position: relative; z-index: 1; width: 100%; padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 120px); }
  .hero-txt { max-width: 560px; }
  .hero h1 { margin: 22px 0 28px; padding: 28px 0; }
  .hero h1 img { width: 100%; max-width: 520px; filter: drop-shadow(0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.35)); }
  .hero .lede { max-width: 32ch; color: var(--on-night); }
  .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 32px; }

  .story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); }
  .story-head h2 { margin-top: 14px; }
  .story-copy { max-width: 62ch; }
  .story-copy p:not(.lede) { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--on-night-muted); }
  .wide { margin: clamp(56px, 8vw, 112px) 0 0; }
  .wide img { width: 100%; max-height: 640px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 20%; }
  .hero2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; margin-top: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); }
  .hero2 .frame { aspect-ratio: 1; }
  .hero2 h3 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .hero2 p { font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 52ch; color: var(--on-night-muted); }

  .head-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr; gap: 24px 64px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .head-row h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 3.1rem); }
  .head-row p.muted { margin: 0; max-width: 46ch; }
  .vols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(20px, 3vw, 44px); }
  .vol .cover { aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(33, 30, 51, .22); }
  .vol h3 { font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
  .small { font-size: 13.5px; }
  .spreads { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(12px, 2vw, 28px); margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px); }
  .spreads figure { margin: 0; }
  .spreads img { width: 100%; mix-blend-mode: multiply; }

  .tone { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: start; }
  blockquote { margin: 0; }
  blockquote p { font: italic 400 clamp(2rem, 4.2vw, 3.6rem)/1.15 var(--serif); color: var(--flame); }
  .tone-copy p { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--on-night-muted); }
  .trio { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(10px, 1.6vw, 20px); margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); }
  .trio .frame { margin: 0; aspect-ratio: 1; }
  .influences { margin-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px); padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .influences p { font: 400 clamp(1.2rem, 1.8vw, 1.45rem)/1.55 var(--serif); max-width: 70ch; margin: 0; }

  .samples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(10px, 1.6vw, 20px); }
  .sample { aspect-ratio: 11 / 16; cursor: zoom-in; }
  .sample img { transition: transform .8s var(--ease); }
  .sample:hover img { transform: scale(1.03); }
  .read-cta { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px); border-block: 1px solid var(--line); }

  .buy-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; }
  .buy-imgs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .buy-imgs figure { margin: 0; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; background: #0d0b0f; }
  .buy-txt h2 { margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .options { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 28px 0 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-light); }
  .options a { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 16px 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-light); transition: background .2s, padding .2s; }
  .options a:hover { background: var(--paper); padding-inline: 12px; }
  .options b { display: block; font: 500 1.35rem/1.2 var(--serif); }
  .price { font: 500 1.2rem/1 var(--serif); white-space: nowrap; color: var(--crimson); }

  .for-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); }
  .for-grid h3 { margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--sky); }
  .aud { margin: 20px 0 0; padding-left: 1.2em; font-size: 1.05rem; display: grid; gap: 10px; color: var(--on-night-muted); }
  .aud li::marker { color: var(--flame); }
  .for-grid p:not(.lede) { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--on-night-muted); }

  .creator { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; }
  .photos { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.33fr 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: end; }
  .photos .frame { margin: 0; }
  .photos .frame:first-child { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  .photos .frame:last-child { aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; }
  .creator h2 { margin: 14px 0 18px; }
  .creator .lede { color: var(--on-night); max-width: 38ch; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .creator p:not(.eyebrow):not(.lede) { max-width: 60ch; color: var(--on-night-muted); }

  .lb { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 200; background: rgba(24, 22, 42, .97); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr 64px; align-items: center; justify-items: center; padding: max(56px, env(safe-area-inset-top)) 0 24px; }
  .lb img { max-height: calc(100dvh - 96px); max-width: 100%; width: auto; object-fit: contain; }
  .lb-x { position: absolute; top: calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px)); right: max(20px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px)); color: var(--on-night); font: 400 12px/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lb-nav { color: var(--on-night); font-size: 44px; height: 100%; width: 100%; }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .story, .hero2, .head-row, .tone, .buy-grid, .for-grid, .creator { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero { min-height: 0; align-items: flex-end; }
    .hero-bg { position: relative; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; object-position: 75% 30%; }
    .hero { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .hero::after { display: none; }
    .hero-bg { -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000 70%, transparent); mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000 70%, transparent); }
    .hero-grid { padding-top: 8px; }
    .hero h1 { margin-top: 12px; }
    .vols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 560px; }
    .vol .cover { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
    .samples { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .spreads, .trio { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .spreads figure:last-child, .trio .frame:last-child { display: none; }
    .samples { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .lb { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .lb-nav { position: absolute; bottom: 12px; width: 56px; height: 56px; } .prev { left: 8px; } .next { right: 8px; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Sample-page lightbox
  const data = JSON.parse(document.querySelector('[data-samples]')!.textContent!);
  const lb = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lb]')!, img = lb.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>('[data-img]')!;
  let cur = 0;
  const show = (i: number) => { cur = (i + data.length) % data.length; img.src = data[cur].src; img.alt = data[cur].alt; };
  const close = () => { lb.hidden = true; document.body.style.overflow = ''; };
  document.querySelector('[data-gal]')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => { const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-i]'); if (!b) return; show(+b.dataset.i!); lb.hidden = false; document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden'; });
  lb.querySelector('[data-x]')!.addEventListener('click', close);
  lb.querySelector('[data-p]')!.addEventListener('click', () => show(cur - 1));
  lb.querySelector('[data-n]')!.addEventListener('click', () => show(cur + 1));
  lb.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if (e.target === lb) close(); });
  addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (lb.hidden) return; if (e.key === 'Escape') close(); if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') show(cur - 1); if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') show(cur + 1); });

  // "Continue reading" when the visitor has read before
  try {
    const last = Number(localStorage.getItem('theseus-last-page'));
    if (last > 1) document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-continue]').forEach((a) => { a.href = `/read/${last}/`; a.textContent = `Continue · page ${last}`; });
  } catch {}
</script>
